        <h2>Extended response ready (learn these “perfect sentences”)</h2>
        <p>These are the kind of points that score marks quickly in extended response answers.</p>

        <details class="panel" open>
          <summary><span>Skeletal system</span><span class="tag">Functions</span></summary>
          <div class="panel-body">
            <ul>
              <li>The skeleton supports muscles and organs and gives the body shape.</li>
              <li>Bones protect delicate organs and provide muscle attachment to allow movement.</li>
              <li>Bone marrow produces blood cells.</li>
              <li><strong>Tendons</strong> connect bone to muscle; <strong>ligaments</strong> connect bone to bone.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="panel" open>
          <summary><span>Respiratory system</span><span class="tag">Gas exchange</span></summary>
          <div class="panel-body">
            <ul>
              <li>Oxygen moves from the air into the lungs and then into the bloodstream; carbon dioxide moves the opposite way.</li>
              <li>Gas exchange happens at the <strong>alveoli</strong> (air sacs) which have thin, moist walls, a large surface area and a good blood supply.</li>
              <li>When you inhale, the diaphragm contracts (moves down) and the chest expands; exhale is the reverse.</li>
              <li>Test for carbon dioxide: <strong>limewater turns cloudy</strong>.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="panel" open>
          <summary><span>Circulatory system</span><span class="tag">Heart + vessels</span></summary>
          <div class="panel-body">
            <ul>
              <li>The heart is made of muscle and <strong>pumps blood</strong> around the body.</li>
              <li><strong>Arteries</strong> carry blood away from the heart and have thick walls; <strong>veins</strong> carry blood back and have valves; <strong>capillaries</strong> are one cell thick for quick exchange.</li>
              <li>Deoxygenated blood goes from the heart to the lungs, gains oxygen, returns to the heart, then oxygenated blood is pumped to the body.</li>
              <li>Valves stop blood flowing backwards.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="panel" open>
          <summary><span>Digestive system</span><span class="tag">Peristalsis</span></summary>
          <div class="panel-body">
            <ul>
              <li>Digestion changes large insoluble food molecules into small soluble molecules that can be absorbed into the bloodstream.</li>
              <li><strong>Peristalsis</strong> is muscle contraction in the oesophagus that pushes food downwards.</li>
              <li>Enzymes speed up the breakdown of food molecules; bile helps break down fats.</li>
              <li>Most nutrients are absorbed in the <strong>small intestine</strong>; water is absorbed in the <strong>large intestine</strong>.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="panel" open>
          <summary><span>Reproduction</span><span class="tag">Key definitions</span></summary>
          <div class="panel-body">
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Reproduction</strong> is producing new life (offspring).</li>
              <li><strong>Sexual reproduction</strong> needs two parents; <strong>asexual reproduction</strong> needs one parent.</li>
              <li>Male organs: testes, sperm duct/tube, penis, urethra, prostate (and seminal vesicle).</li>
              <li>Female organs: ovaries, oviduct, uterus, cervix, vagina.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="panel" open>
          <summary><span>Fertilisation + pregnancy</span><span class="tag">Zygote</span></summary>
          <div class="panel-body">
            <ul>
              <li>Sex cells in humans are <strong>sperm</strong> and <strong>egg</strong>.</li>
              <li><strong>Ovulation</strong> is when an egg is released (about every 28 days).</li>
              <li><strong>Fertilisation</strong> is fusion of the sperm nucleus and egg nucleus to form a <strong>zygote</strong>.</li>
              <li>The zygote travels to the uterus and <strong>implants</strong> in the uterus wall.</li>
              <li>Pregnancy lasts about <strong>40 weeks</strong> and is split into three trimesters.</li>
              <li>The placenta allows exchange of food/oxygen/waste between mother and baby; the umbilical cord connects baby to placenta.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="panel">
          <summary><span>Risks to the baby</span><span class="tag">Safety</span></summary>
          <div class="panel-body">
            <ul>
              <li>Harmful chemicals from <strong>smoking</strong>, <strong>alcohol</strong> and certain <strong>drugs</strong> can pass from the mother’s bloodstream to the baby.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>

      <!-- CHECKLIST + PROGRESS -->
      <div class="card" id="checklist">
        <h2>Revision checklist (tap to track)</h2>
        <p class="muted">Tick as you revise. Your progress saves on this device.</p>

        <div class="checklist" id="revList" aria-label="Revision checklist"></div>

        <div class="progress" aria-label="Progress indicator">
          <div id="progText" style="font-weight:900;"></div>
          <div class="bar"><div id="progBar"></div></div>
          <button class="btn wide" type="button" id="resetTicks">Reset ticks</button>
        </div>
      </div>

    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div>© Mr Stewart’s Science • S2 Biology</div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    // ============================
    // Drawer: open/close + overlay click + ESC + focus trap
    // ============================
    const menuBtn = document.getElementById('menuBtn');
    const drawer = document.getElementById('siteDrawer');
    const overlay = document.getElementById('overlay');
    const closeLink = document.getElementById('closeDrawerLink');

    let lastFocused = null;

    function getFocusable(container){
      return Array.from(container.querySelectorAll(
        'a[href], button:not([disabled]), [tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"]), summary'
      )).filter(el => !el.hasAttribute('disabled'));
    }

    function openDrawer(){
      lastFocused = document.activeElement;
      drawer.classList.add('open');
      drawer.setAttribute('aria-hidden','false');
      overlay.hidden = false;
      menuBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded','true');
      document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';

      const focusables = getFocusable(drawer);
      if(focusables.length) focusables[0].focus();
    }

    function closeDrawer(){
      drawer.classList.remove('open');
      drawer.setAttribute('aria-hidden','true');
      overlay.hidden = true;
      menuBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false');
      document.body.style.overflow = '';

      if(lastFocused && typeof lastFocused.focus === 'function') lastFocused.focus();
    }

    menuBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      drawer.classList.contains('open') ? closeDrawer() : openDrawer();
    });

    closeLink.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      closeDrawer();
    });

    overlay.addEventListener('click', closeDrawer);

    document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if(e.key === 'Escape' && drawer.classList.contains('open')) closeDrawer();

      if(e.key === 'Tab' && drawer.classList.contains('open')){
        const focusables = getFocusable(drawer);
        if(!focusables.length) return;

        const first = focusables[0];
        const last = focusables[focusables.length - 1];

        if(e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === first){
          e.preventDefault(); last.focus();
        } else if(!e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === last){
          e.preventDefault(); first.focus();
        }
      }
    });

    // ============================
    // Revision checklist + progress (localStorage)
    // ============================
    const KEY = "s2bio_body_repro_revcheck_v1";
    const tasks = [
      "Read KO: Skeletal system (functions + tendons/ligaments)",
      "Read KO: Respiratory system (alveoli + gas exchange)",
      "Read KO: Circulatory system (heart + arteries/veins/capillaries)",
      "Read KO: Digestive system (peristalsis + enzymes + absorption)",
      "Read KO: Reproduction organs (male + female)",
      "Read KO: Fertilisation (ovulation → zygote → implantation)",
      "Read KO: Pregnancy + placenta + umbilical cord",
      "Flashcards (10 mins)",
      "Practice questions (at least 10)",
      "Do one timed 30 minute run-through"
    ];

    const list = document.getElementById("revList");
    const progText = document.getElementById("progText");
    const progBar = document.getElementById("progBar");
    const reset = document.getElementById("resetTicks");

    function load(){
      try{
        const raw = localStorage.getItem(KEY);
        if(!raw) return Array(tasks.length).fill(false);
        const arr = JSON.parse(raw);
        if(!Array.isArray(arr) || arr.length !== tasks.length) return Array(tasks.length).fill(false);
        return arr.map(Boolean);
      }catch{
        return Array(tasks.length).fill(false);
      }
    }
    function save(state){
      try{ localStorage.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify(state)); }catch{}
    }

    function render(){
      const state = load();
      list.innerHTML = "";

      state.forEach((checked, i) => {
        const label = document.createElement("label");
        const cb = document.createElement("input");
        cb.type = "checkbox";
        cb.checked = checked;

        cb.addEventListener("change", () => {
          const next = load();
          next[i] = cb.checked;
          save(next);
          render();
        });

        const span = document.createElement("span");
        span.textContent = tasks[i];
        span.style.lineHeight = "1.35";
        span.style.color = "rgba(255,255,255,0.92)";

        label.appendChild(cb);
        label.appendChild(span);
        list.appendChild(label);
      });

      const done = state.filter(Boolean).length;
      const total = tasks.length;
      const pct = total ? Math.round((done/total)*100) : 0;

      progText.textContent = `You’ve completed ${done} / ${total} tasks (${pct}%).`;
      progBar.style.width = pct + "%";
    }

    reset.addEventListener("click", () => {
      save(Array(tasks.length).fill(false));
      render();
    });

    render();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
